# Home Cleaning

Source: [Home Cleaning](https://beachlinecleaners.com/residential-cleaning/)

We handle the routine cleaning—kitchens, bathrooms, floors, dusting, and living areas—whether you need a one-time clean or regular weekly or biweekly service.

## What’s included in a standard clean

This is the core home-cleaning checklist. If you need something beyond it, we can add that to the quote—no extras are required.

- Kitchen counters, sink, cabinet fronts, appliance exteriors, and floors
- Bathroom toilets, showers, tubs, sinks, mirrors, counters, fixtures, and floors
- Dusting reachable surfaces and cleaning mirrors in bedrooms and living areas
- Vacuuming and mopping appropriate floor surfaces
- Trash removal and basic room reset

## Who this is for

Book a one-time clean to catch up, or choose weekly or biweekly visits for routine upkeep.

## Options & Add-ons

Need a little more done? Appliance interiors, empty cabinet interiors, and interior windows can be added to your quote. If you only need the standard clean, leave the extras off.

- Inside refrigerator and oven
- Inside cabinets (if emptied)
- Interior windows

## What affects the price

From $125 per visit

We base the quote on the size of the home, bedrooms and bathrooms, current condition, and how often you want service. If there’s heavier buildup, we may recommend starting with a deep clean before moving to regular maintenance.

Starting prices give you a ballpark. We’ll confirm the actual price before you book based on the property, its condition, cleaning frequency, and any extras you want.

- Square footage
- Bedrooms & bathrooms
- Condition & buildup
- Cleaning frequency

## Service FAQs

### What should I do before you arrive?

You don’t need to clean first. Pick up loose items, clothing, and toys, and clear dishes from the sink so we can reach the surfaces and floors. Tell us about pets, delicate surfaces, or product preferences. We’ll arrange access ahead of time. If cabinet interiors are included in your clean, empty them before we arrive.

### What isn’t included in a standard home clean?

Standard cleaning covers reachable surfaces. Baseboard and trim detailing are part of a deep clean. Appliance interiors, empty cabinet interiors, and interior windows are optional extras. Moving heavy furniture or appliances, organizing clutter, washing dishes, and laundry are outside the standard home-cleaning checklist. Rental laundry and restocking can be arranged separately.

### Do I need to be home?

Either is fine. If you’ll be out, we’ll agree on secure property access before the appointment.

### Do you bring supplies?

We bring standard cleaning supplies and equipment for routine service. If your home has delicate surfaces, product preferences, or sensitivities, tell us before the visit.

### What if I have pets?

Pets are welcome. If your pet may become anxious, act aggressively, or get in the way, please keep them in a secure area during the clean.

